Consider elastic electron–hadron scattering e^± + h → e^± + h (and the time-like crossed process e^+e^- ↔ h\bar h), where the leading QED amplitude is one-photon exchange (1γ) and the next-order contribution is two-photon exchange (2γ). In the Born (1γ-only) approximation, the unpolarized cross section satisfies the linear Rosenbluth form in the virtual-photon polarization parameter ε, the electron–proton and positron–proton cross sections are equal, the recoil polarization components determine the form-factor ratio G_E/G_M without contamination, and certain single-spin observables vanish by time-reversal invariance.

Identify a complete set of experimentally measurable quantities whose deviation from the Born predictions provides unambiguous signatures of two-photon exchange (or 1γ⊗2γ interference). Specifically, determine:

(a) which features of the unpolarized Rosenbluth (reduced) cross section as a function of ε at fixed Q² (e.g., departures from linearity) signal 2γ contributions;

(b) which ratios or differences of e^- h and e^+ h elastic cross sections isolate the 1γ⊗2γ interference (the charge-odd part) versus the charge-even 1γ² + 2γ² part;

(c) which polarization observables — including the longitudinal and transverse recoil polarization components P_L, P_T (and their ratio used to extract G_E/G_M), induced normal target/recoil polarizations, and beam–target spin asymmetries — carry T-odd or Born-forbidden pieces that are nonzero only in the presence of 2γ exchange;

(d) the analogous set of observables in the time-like region (e^+e^- → h\bar h or h\bar h → e^+e^-), in particular angular asymmetries of the produced hadron with respect to the beam axis (forward–backward asymmetry) and single-spin asymmetries normal to the scattering plane, that are forbidden in the 1γ approximation and hence diagnose 2γ exchange.

Provide for each observable the symmetry argument (C, P, T, or crossing) that makes it a clean signature, and indicate the kinematic dependence (on Q² and ε, or equivalently scattering angle) expected for a 2γ-dominated or 1γ⊗2γ-interference contribution.

